<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">
    <!--
        Vector icons extracted from Fluent UI System Icons so the app no longer depends on
        the FluentIcons.Avalonia NuGet package. Render these with a PathIcon, which fills the
        geometry with the control's Foreground (so theme colors keep flowing through
        DynamicResource exactly as the old SymbolIcon did):

            <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource IconSettings}" Width="16" Height="16"/>

        These are the 16px Regular variants (viewBox 0 0 16 16) — authored for small UI with
        proportionally thicker strokes, so they stay crisp at icon sizes. Render them at 16x16
        (1:1 with the source grid) for the sharpest result; the global PathIcon style in
        Controls.axaml adds UseLayoutRounding so edges snap to the pixel grid. Power has no
        16px variant, so it uses the 20px one (viewBox 0 0 20 20) — PathIcon stretches Uniform
        to fit regardless, so the mixed grid is fine.

        The leading "F1" sets the non-zero fill rule, matching the SVG source so glyphs with
        holes (gear, save, folder, pin) render correctly.
    -->

